diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..f04f0c7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,31 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Browser tools (WebMCP)
+
+The shared header exposes client-side tools to browser agents through the React
+`use-webmcp-tool` integration. Browsers without WebMCP keep the regular UI.
+
+| Tool | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `open_article_search` | Open the search flyout, exposing its `search_articles` form tool. |
+| `open_reading_list` | Open the reading-list flyout, exposing its `update_reading_list` form tool. |
+| `find_articles` | Search article titles and summaries using `query`. |
+| `get_article` | Retrieve article metadata and its URL using `slug`. |
+| `get_reading_list` | Retrieve saved articles for the current session. |
+| `toggle_reading_list` | Save or remove an article using `slug`, returning the resulting list and saved state. |
+
+The form tools are available while their flyouts are open. Both use named,
+validated controls and return results through `SubmitEvent.respondWith` for
+agent submissions. Search accepts `query`; reading-list updates accept `slug`.
+The reading-list form and toggle utility both toggle membership, so invoking
+either twice restores the original state. All reading-list changes use the
+existing session API and update visible bookmarks and the open list.
+
+Imperative tools are registered after hydration and cleaned up on unmount,
+including Astro page transitions. Network tools forward the execution's abort
+signal and return actionable errors. API requests respect Astro's base path.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
